Performance improvement: LAN quick wins — disable depth opacity, 60Hz patches, bullet/geom interpolation.

This commit modifies 5 files (+598/-53 lines), spanning 1 Markdown docs, 1 documentation, 1 game server.
This performance commit improves runtime efficiency. The game targets 60fps on typical hardware with complex enemy AI, instanced mesh rendering, and real-time physics on non-Euclidean surfaces.

Additional context from the commit body:
4 fixes from deep LAN audit (decisions/lan-deep-audit-2026-02-11.md):

1. Disabled depth-based opacity in network mode (was 250+ material
   updates/frame for 50 enemies = massive GPU state churn)
2. Increased server patch rate from 30Hz to 60Hz (setPatchRate 33→16)
3. Added bullet + geom interpolation in onRender (same smooth lerp
   pattern as enemies/players, eliminates 30Hz stutter)
4. Gated diagnostic API behind ?debug URL parameter (200ms polling
   interval no longer runs in production play)

